dialect protocol
protocol binary.mutations
version 1
schema stdio.binary
start record

# P2-P3: real binary op frame -- CONFIRMED ALREADY REAL, not a text-as-binary shortcut needing
# upgrade (per this program's own W0 census: `binary` is one of the 13 stdio standards whose
# `OpBinary::encode_op` already routes through `dsl::variants_binary::encode_op`/`decode_op`, the
# generic handcrafted-once-in-the-framework `format u8 (=1) | variant ordinal varint | record body`
# layout, confirmed by direct read of `🧬️mutations/🦀️component.rs`'s `impl protocol::OpBinary for
# BinaryMutation` -- pure forward calls, zero per-artifact logic). `record body` is
# `store::pack_rt::encode_record_body` -- the CONTAINER-LESS twin of the full `.spk` document
# format (no magic/header/manifest/footer): `symbol_count varint, (len varint, utf8 bytes)*
# symbols, then the record's own fields`. `BinaryMutation`'s fields (`offset`/`remove_len: usize`,
# `insert`/`data: Vec<u8>`, and `SetSnapshot`'s nested `BinarySnapshot` block) are NOT a
# self-recursive/data-carrying-enum type (unlike json/csv's `JsonValue`/`JsonPath`), but
# `Prim::Ref` still unconditionally errors on ANY struct/enum-shaped field during `walk_protocol`
# (confirmed unchanged since P2-M2, same root cause every other pilot's `mechanism_gaps` entry
# cites) -- so the record body's own internal field-by-field shape is not further
# protocol-walkable here either; it stays one opaque trailing chain, exactly json/csv's own
# treatment of their (differently-shaped, but equally protocol-opaque) recursive payloads. The two
# REAL fixed-shape leading fields (`format`, the variant `ordinal`) ARE protocol-walkable and
# modeled here field-by-field.
framing record
header fixed 2
field format u8
field ordinal varint
chain body bytes
